{
  "case_id": "2019-18-1584",
  "document_hash": "98179207626d901fbf9bce66fe3a35e915c90a205dd4687238883d2528680073",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1584",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "98179207626d901fbf9bce66fe3a35e915c90a205dd4687238883d2528680073",
      "evidence_id": "ev-98179207626d-0000-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: We'll hear argument first this morning in Case 18-1584, the United States Forest Service versus Cowpasture River Preservation Association, and the consolidated case."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Cowpasture River Preservation Association",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1584",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "98179207626d901fbf9bce66fe3a35e915c90a205dd4687238883d2528680073",
      "evidence_id": "ev-98179207626d-0000-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 7,
        "start": 6
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Respondents' theory is inconsistent with the Act and would dramatically change the national trail system. Respondents, for instance, argue that the trail is land and it's administered by the Park Service."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1584",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "98179207626d901fbf9bce66fe3a35e915c90a205dd4687238883d2528680073",
      "evidence_id": "ev-98179207626d-0000-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: But then what do we make of the line in the reply brief that says \"no one doubts that the trail is in the National Park System\"?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1584",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "98179207626d901fbf9bce66fe3a35e915c90a205dd4687238883d2528680073",
      "evidence_id": "ev-98179207626d-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "the question was what harm would we do if we just\nrestrict this to the question that answers it,"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Atlantic Coast Pipeline",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1584",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "98179207626d901fbf9bce66fe3a35e915c90a205dd4687238883d2528680073",
      "evidence_id": "ev-98179207626d-0001-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 28,
        "start": 28
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "our reply brief, that generally speaking if you\ngrant a right-of-way, which is one way of\nthinking about the trail, it doesn't affect\nsubsurface rights. So that actually does\nsupport this way of thinking about it."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1584",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "98179207626d901fbf9bce66fe3a35e915c90a205dd4687238883d2528680073",
      "evidence_id": "ev-98179207626d-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: When the statute says\nthat the Park System consists of lands\nadministered by the Park Service, does it mean\nadministered in full, administered exclusively\nby the Park Service, or administered in any\nsense by the Park Service?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Respondents",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1584",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "98179207626d901fbf9bce66fe3a35e915c90a205dd4687238883d2528680073",
      "evidence_id": "ev-98179207626d-0001-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "ORAL ARGUMENT OF MICHAEL K. KELLOGG\nON BEHALF OF THE RESPONDENTS\nMR. KELLOGG: Mr. Chief Justice, and\nmay it please the Court:\nI want to go directly to the question\nof whether there's an easy out in this case by\nsaying it's 600 feet under the ground, so it\ndoesn't count. I'll call the Court's attention\nto 1248(a), which specifically says that rights\nof ways are to be granted by the Secretary of\nthe Interior in this case for anything,\n\"rights-of-ways upon, over, under, across, or\nalong any components\" of the Appalachian Trail.\nSo \"under\" counts, as Justice Kagan\npointed out, the Mineral Leasing Act itself\ntalks about who has jurisdiction over the\nsurface lands."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1584",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "98179207626d901fbf9bce66fe3a35e915c90a205dd4687238883d2528680073",
      "evidence_id": "ev-98179207626d-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 45,
        "start": 45
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: Okay. What's the answer?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "MR. KELLOGG",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1584",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "98179207626d901fbf9bce66fe3a35e915c90a205dd4687238883d2528680073",
      "evidence_id": "ev-98179207626d-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. KELLOGG: Because the Mineral Leasing Act only applies to federal land, and it only exempts land in the National Park Service from the definition of federal land."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1584",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "98179207626d901fbf9bce66fe3a35e915c90a205dd4687238883d2528680073",
      "evidence_id": "ev-98179207626d-0002-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 61,
        "start": 61
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Affirm?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1584",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "98179207626d901fbf9bce66fe3a35e915c90a205dd4687238883d2528680073",
      "evidence_id": "ev-98179207626d-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Excuse me, Mr. Yang --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2019-18-1584",
      "confidence": 0.96,
      "document_hash": "98179207626d901fbf9bce66fe3a35e915c90a205dd4687238883d2528680073",
      "evidence_id": "ev-98179207626d-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: The case is submitted."
    },
